Wave 15, lane D -- do not pre-instantiate the quest bazaar screen.

Lane B's wall (docs/spikes/cheerpj-assets.md §5): Forge's boot dies in
forge.util.IgnoringXStream.<init>, reached from QuestBazaarManager.load <-
VBazaarUI.populateStalls <- FView.cacheUIStates. XStream's
com.thoughtworks.xstream.core.JVM.<clinit> self-tests the unsafe reflection
provider, CheerpJ ships no Java_jdk_internal_misc_Unsafe_putChar, and the
resulting UnsatisfiedLinkError is an Error rather than an Exception, so
XStream's own guard does not catch it and the class is poisoned for the life of
the JVM.

Lane B named "does a match-only client touch XStream at all?" as the free thing
to try first. It does not: XStream appears in exactly three areas of Forge --
quest (incl. bazaar), gauntlet and tournament -- and a Constructed match path
enters none of them. `grep -rl XStream` over the tree lists only
gamemodes/quest/**, gamemodes/gauntlet/**, gamemodes/tournament/**,
util/IgnoringXStream.java and one desktop test.

cacheUIStates() pre-builds three screens at startup purely to warm them. Two of
them (home, deck editor) are on our path; the bazaar is a quest-mode screen this
product would never show. Not instantiating it eagerly is the smallest change
that clears the wall, and it is a change we would want anyway.

The import goes too, and not as tidiness: forge-gui-desktop runs
maven-checkstyle-plugin at validate with UnusedImports as an ERROR, so leaving
it turns a working patch into a BUILD FAILURE. Measured -- the first version of
this patch kept the import "because an unused import is a warning, not an
error", and Checkstyle 10.18.2 failed the build on exactly that line.

